{
  "summary": "The experiment tested a multiprofile RNA-only model using the scvi_n200 RNA encoder with average pooling aggregation, achieving validation accuracy of 0.6501 and F1 of 0.6275, outperforming the pca_n2000-based multiprofile baseline (0.5907 accuracy). This suggests the RNA encoder choice may influence performance in multiprofile settings, but the relative impact of aggregation methods versus encoder type remains uncertain due to limited direct comparisons. Further experiments are needed to isolate these factors and validate trends across different modalities."
}

